# GitHub Personal Access Token — used by the gh CLI inside the devcontainer.
#
# Create a fine-grained PAT scoped to only this repository:
#   https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
#
# Recommended permissions (repository-scoped):
#   Contents:      Read and write  (read code, create branches)
#   Pull requests: Read and write  (open, comment on, merge PRs)
#   Issues:        Read and write  (if you use GitHub issues)
#   Metadata:      Read-only       (required by GitHub, auto-included)
#   Actions:       Read-only       (view CI run status)
#
# Keep it scoped to one repo and set an expiry. If the token leaks, an attacker
# can only touch this one repository.
GH_TOKEN=
